From: Holodor <holodor@bonesaw.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] serial: qcom-geni: drop the sleep-set votes of every open port across suspend

qcom_geni_serial_suspend() switches the console port's interconnect votes to
QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY "so we can hit the lowest possible state in
suspend".  Every other port that is open across suspend has the same
problem: uart_suspend_port() shuts it down and drops its UART_PM_STATE, but
that only does a runtime PM put, which cannot suspend the device while the
PM core holds it from prepare to complete.  The port stays powered with its
ALWAYS-tagged votes in the RPMh sleep set.

On the Retroid Pocket 5 the gamepad MCU (serdev on 888000.serial) and the
QCA6390 Bluetooth (serdev on 998000.serial) are open all the time; at every
suspend flush their votes kept QUP0 at 2000/2000, CN0 at 150/150 and SN11
on, and with both UARTs closed for a test those BCMs left the sleep set.
Apply the console's tag switch to every port.
---
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c	2026-10-16 13:25:03.218283676 +0900
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c	2026-10-16 13:25:03.234696428 +0900
@@ -1977,12 +1977,15 @@
 
 	/*
 	 * This is done so we can hit the lowest possible state in suspend
-	 * even with no_console_suspend
+	 * even with no_console_suspend, and for every other port that stays
+	 * open across suspend (serdev clients such as Bluetooth or a gamepad
+	 * MCU): uart_suspend_port() shuts the port down, but its runtime PM
+	 * put cannot power it off while the PM core holds the device from
+	 * prepare to complete, so the ALWAYS-tagged interconnect votes would
+	 * stay in the RPMh sleep set and keep the QUP/NoC/DDR BCMs on.
 	 */
-	if (uart_console(uport)) {
-		geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY);
-		geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
-	}
+	geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY);
+	geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
 	return uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
 }
 
@@ -1994,10 +1997,8 @@
 	struct qcom_geni_private_data *private_data = uport->private_data;
 
 	ret = uart_resume_port(private_data->drv, uport);
-	if (uart_console(uport)) {
-		geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS);
-		geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
-	}
+	geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS);
+	geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
 	return ret;
 }
 
